1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,800
Hi, George! Glad you're back, Loads of people have phoned you.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,580
Really? - I felt just like your secretary!

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:13,114
Sorry! I went into the library this afternoon to have a look at a newspaper

4
00:00:13,114 --> 00:00:15,230
and I came across something really interesting.

5
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:19,080
What? A book? - No, a brochure from a summer festival

6
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,800
mainly Spanish music. Look, I've got it here.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,600
Spanish music? I really love the guitar.

8
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:31,430
Let's have a look. So what's this group 'Guitarrini'?

9
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:33,468
They're really good. They had a video

10
00:00:33,468 --> 00:00:39,290
with all the highlights of the festival at a stand in the lobby to the library, so I heard them.

11
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:44,600
They play fantastic instruments - drums and flutes and old kinds of guitars.

12
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,670
I've never heard anything like it before. - Sounds great.

13
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:53,370
Okay. Shall we go then? Spoil ourselves? - Yes, let's.

14
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:57,960
The only problem is there aren't any cheap seats, it's all one price.

15
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:04,310
Well, in that case we could sit right at the front - we'd have a really good view.

16
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:06,340
Yeah. though I think that

17
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:09,260
if you sit at the back you can actually hear the whole thing better.

18
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:14,270
Yes. Anyway we can decide when we get there.

19
00:01:14,270 --> 00:01:18,040
So will you fill in the form or shall I?

20
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:26,830
I'll do it. Name: Georcle O'Neill. Address: 48 North Avenue, Westsea.

21
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:30,570
Do you remember our new postcode? Still can't remember it.

22
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:41,400
Just a minute - I've got it written down here. WS6 2YH. Do you need the phone too?

23
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:44,230
Please. I'm really bad at numbers.

24
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:55,230
01674 553242. So, let's book two tickets for Guitarrini.

25
00:01:55,230 --> 00:02:00,080
Okay. If you're sure £7.50 each is all right. How do you feel about the singer?

26
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:06,720
I haven't quite decided. But I've noticed something on the booking form that might just persuade me!

27
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:09,980
What's that then? - Free refreshments! - Really?

28
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:18,230
Yes, look here. Sunday 17th of June. Singer, ticket £6.00 includes drinks in the garden.

29
00:02:18,230 --> 00:02:19,880
Sounds like a bargain to me!

30
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:22,910
Yes, let's book two tickets for that.

31
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:26,940
So, what else? I'm feeling quite keen now!

32
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,800
How about the pianist on the 22nd of June?

33
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,200
Anna Ventura? I've just remembered that's my evening class night.

34
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:37,117
That's okay. I'll just have to go on my own -

35
00:02:37,117 --> 00:02:41,200
but we can go to the Spanish dance and guitar concert together, can't we?

36
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:46,660
Yes - I'm sure Tom and Kieran would enjoy that too. Good heavens - £10.50 a ticket!

37
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:51,060
I can see we're going to have to go without food for the rest of the week

38
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:52,840
we'll need to book four!

39
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:55,680
Wish we were students - look

40
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:01,360
Children, Students and Senior Citizens get a 50% discount on everything.

41
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,510
If only!
